@startuml US11 use case diagram
' US11 REST verification, use case diagram v0.1. Same system and actors as the US10 diagram;
' US10 use cases faded grey, US11 use cases in green.

title US11 use case diagram (REST verification)

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam usecase {
    BackgroundColor white
    BorderColor #999999
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF4DA
    BorderColor #D8C9A3
}
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor Developer as dev
actor "API client\n(browser or own app)" as client
actor "REST API server\n(the developer's application)" as server

rectangle "ZAP with REST Extraction add-on" {
    ' US10, context only
    usecase "Add API namespace" as UC1 #F6F6F6;line:DDDDDD;text:A8A8A8
    usecase "Register endpoint pattern" as UC2 #F6F6F6;line:DDDDDD;text:A8A8A8
    usecase "Start / stop extraction" as UC3 #F6F6F6;line:DDDDDD;text:A8A8A8
    usecase "View API report" as UC4 #F6F6F6;line:DDDDDD;text:A8A8A8
    usecase "Send request through proxy\n(existing ZAP)" as SEND #F6F6F6;line:DDDDDD;text:A8A8A8
    usecase "Record matching API call" as REC #F6F6F6;line:DDDDDD;text:A8A8A8

    ' US11
    usecase "UC-V1 Define the spec\nof an endpoint" as V1 #C8E6C9;line:2E7D32;line.bold
    usecase "UC-V2 Verify traffic\nagainst the spec" as V2 #C8E6C9;line:2E7D32;line.bold
    usecase "UC-V3 Inspect the verification\nresult of a call" as V3 #C8E6C9;line:2E7D32;line.bold
    usecase "UC-V4 Read the compliance\ndocumentation" as V4 #C8E6C9;line:2E7D32;line.bold
    usecase "UC-V5 Add an endpoint pattern\nfrom an unmatched path" as V5 #C8E6C9;line:2E7D32;line.bold
}

dev -[#CCCCCC]- UC1
dev -[#CCCCCC]- UC2
dev -[#CCCCCC]- UC3
dev -[#CCCCCC]- UC4
dev -[#2E7D32,bold]- V1
dev -[#2E7D32,bold]- V3
dev -[#2E7D32,bold]- V4
dev -[#2E7D32,bold]- V5
client -[#CCCCCC]- SEND
SEND -[#CCCCCC]- server

REC .[#CCCCCC].> SEND : <color:#A8A8A8><<extend>></color>
V2 .[#2E7D32,bold].> REC : <color:#1B5E20><<extend>></color>
V3 .[#2E7D32,bold].> UC4 : <color:#1B5E20><<extend>></color>
V4 .[#2E7D32,bold].> UC4 : <color:#1B5E20><<extend>></color>
V5 .[#2E7D32,bold].> UC2 : <color:#1B5E20><<include>></color>

note right of V2
    Extension point in Record matching API call:
    call recorded. Condition: the endpoint has a
    non-empty spec. Verification itself happens
    when the report is made (D2), so UC-V2 also
    runs again after every spec change.
end note

note left of V1
    Precondition: the endpoint pattern is registered.
    Its spec starts empty (D8).
end note

note right of V5
    Secondary (D4). Uses the paths that a started
    namespace saw but no pattern matched.
end note

@enduml
